    "summary": "Turn 50 reviewed the executor-timeout check, whose outcome is holds, closing the liveness question.\n\nState on entry. Claim C8-timeout-enqueues-blocked-instance has one artifact, 037aa44cdea4453abcd4f9d4439d1dee (executed as f01d61d7…), whose monitor outcome is holds with the oracle correspondence unreviewed. The trusted runner reproduced the observation: the prerequisite (status 0, no commands, crtInstance 0, ExecedUpTo -1) and then recovery_enqueued with enqueued true, enqueued_replica 1, enqueued_instance 0 after about 12.6 seconds. Claim C7 was confirmed this cycle as well, so the dead accept-rejection path is settled.\n\nReview judgement (checker_correspondence, no_issue_found). Requirement versus predicate: the claim is that a blocked instance must be enqueued for recovery once the executor's grace period elapses, and the predicate asserts enqueued == true, with the enqueued replica and instance fields independently corroborating which operation was admitted. Entry and schedule: the blocked record is built with the package's own constructor in the state a replica reaches when it has an instance number but no committed commands, the executor goroutine is the implementation's own loop started directly instead of by New(), and the harness reads instancesToRecover rather than letting the run loop consume it; the prerequisite prints the fields that would reveal an unreached premise. Oracle and identity: the comparison is against whether the channel received the instance, sharing identity with the prerequisite. Observation path and completion: the select has a bounded alternative that prints enqueued false, so a non-observation would be recorded rather than hidden, and the goroutine ends through the harness's deferred Shutdown flag. Limits are explicit: the measured wait follows the loop's per-iteration counter rather than a clock, so it is a diagnostic; only the enqueue is observed, not the recovery that consumes it; one blocked row is exercised; and the executor was started by the harness rather than by epaxos.New.\n\nEffect on the run's picture. The progress path that the dead rejection branch (C7) relies on is now established by observation, with the delay a stalled row actually incurs measured at roughly 12.6 seconds instead of cited from the constant. Audit spec version 11; the eight settled claims (seven confirmed or bounded, one pending this review) and the two paused candidates are untouched, and the only visible bookkeeping item remains the scope issue on the superseded C1 artifact. No requirement, premise or earlier observation was weakened."
